        "visibleWords": "Skip to content\nPORTFOLIO\nPROJECTS\nEXPERIENCE\nHACKATHONS\nEDUCATION\nRESUME\n2028\n3RD\nJoshua Aryeetey\nOPEN TO SUMMER 2027\nEducation\n\nTORONTO METROPOLITAN UNIVERSITY\n\nComputer Engineering\n\nSoftware Specialization · B.Eng.\n\nExpected 2028\n\nDental Clinic DBMS\n\nCURRENT · IN PROGRESS\n\nEVIDENCE PENDING\n\nBookstore Management System\n\nEVIDENCE PENDING\n\nQuartus/VHDL 8-bit ALU and nine-state FSM lab project\nFour-stage CMOS amplifier\n\nEVIDENCE PENDING\n\nQUARTUS II · CYCLONE II · LAB 6 · PART 2\n\nAn opcode-driven ALU and controller\nDATA PATH\nA and B · 8-bit inputs\n\nTwo latch1 input registers\n\nCONTROL PATH\nNine-state Moore FSM\n\nCurrent state passes through a one-hot opcode decoder\n\n→\nPROCESS\nClocked 8-bit ALU\n\nLatched operands + 16-bit opcode\n\n→\nDISPLAY PATH\nR1 and R2 · 4-bit nibbles\n\nSent to seven-segment decoders\n\nSource-derived from the configured Lab 6 part 2 block diagram; the separate identifier-display branch is omitted.\nNINE OPCODE BRANCHES\nShift A right by two with 1-fill\n(A - B) + 4\nMaximum of A and B\nConcatenate B's low nibble with A's high nibble\nIncrement A\nBitwise AND\nInvert A's high nibble\nRotate B left by three\nZero result\nSTATE PROGRESSION\n\nWhen data_in is high on a rising clock edge, the FSM advances; when low, it holds. The sequence wraps from state s9 to s1, and the component's reset input returns it to s1. Its four-bit state feeds a decoder that generates the ALU's one-hot operation input.\n\nThis page describes the selected Quartus source snapshot; it does not claim a hardware demonstration. In this version, the ALU assigns its declared Neg output low on each rising edge and no opcode branch raises it, so no signed-result behavior is claimed.\n\nACTIVITY\n\nGENERAL · PORTFOLIO\n\nCURRENT FOCUS\nCurrent Coursework\nPROJECTS (4)\nFood Tracker\nCho’Veigo\nCrest\nFraymakers\nEXPERIENCE (2)\nLiving in Silico\nStush Patties\nGitHub\nLinkedIn\nX\n✉\nHELP"
      },
